  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "The international mile: a unit of length precisely equal to 1.609344 kilometers established by treaty among Anglophone nations in 1959, divided into 5,280 feet or 1,760 yards."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "Any of several customary units of length derived from the 1593 English statute mile of 8 furlongs, equivalent to 5,280 feet or 1,760 yards of various precise values."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "Any of many customary units of length derived from the Roman mile (mille passus) of 8 stades or 5,000 Roman feet."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "The Scandinavian mile: a unit of length precisely equal to 10 kilometers defined in 1889."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "Any of many customary units of length from other measurement systems of roughly similar values, as the Chinese (里) or Arabic mile (al-mīl)."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "(travel) An airline mile in a frequent flier program."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "Any similarly large distance."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "A race of 1 mile's length; a race of around 1 mile's length (usually 1500 or 1600 meters)"
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
    part_of_speech noun
    gloss "One mile per hour, as a measure of speed."
    provenance (wiktionary)
  sense
